B.a06=new A.a6("AutoSense AI \u2022 Development version\nPublisher: Youssef Ahmed\nSupport: Support contact pending store release\nPrivacy policy: Public policy URL pending store release\n\nYour choices\nThe demo and live scanner dashboard run on your device. Bluetooth discovery uses nearby device names and identifiers to connect to the scanner you select. On older Android versions, Bluetooth discovery requires a location permission; AutoSense does not request GPS coordinates. Wi-Fi mode connects to the adapter address you enter.\n\nDiagnostic requests\nWhen you request guidance, the app sends your selected vehicle, DTC codes, symptoms, safety selections, notes and input source to the configured backend. Code lookup sends the requested code. Do not enter names, contact details or other personal information in notes. The supplied backend processes requests in memory; hosting providers may process connection metadata and logs.\n\nStorage and sharing\nHistory and recorded runs are kept in app memory and disappear when the app process ends. Reports or CSV data you copy are placed on your device clipboard. This version has no accounts, ads, analytics or enabled cloud history.\n\nSubscriptions\nIn a billing-enabled Google Play build, Google handles checkout. Purchase tokens are sent to the configured backend to verify subscription status and expiry. AutoSense does not collect card details. Development builds keep checkout disabled.\n\nControls\nYou can disconnect a scanner, cancel a run, revoke permissions in Android Settings, and close the app to end its session.\n\nRelease status\nA public support email and hosted privacy-policy URL must be configured before store release. Hardware compatibility is experimental. Guidance lists possibilities, not definite diagnoses. Run estimates are not measured engine horsepower or torque. Real code clearing is disabled.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
